rem Triangles with integral sides and an
rem integral angle
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=279
rem Count the integer sided triangles
rem with a perimeter up to Limit and an
rem angle of a whole number of degrees

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

arg Limit integer = 100000000

rem Only 60, 90 and 120 degrees have a
rem rational cosine among integral
rem angles strictly between 0 and 180.
rem Coprime m > n, with m - n not a
rem multiple of 3, give one primitive
rem 120-degree triangle with sides
rem x=m^2-n^2, y=2mn+n^2, z=m^2+mn+n^2.
rem The triangles (x,x+y,z) and (y,x+y,z)
rem have 60 degrees. Their perimeters
rem are (2m+n)(m+n), 3m(m+n), and
rem (2m+n)(m+2n). Each has Limit // p
rem multiples. Add equilateral ones too.
rem Right triangles need m - n odd and
rem perimeter 2m(m+n). This is smaller
rem than all three other perimeters,
rem so one bound and gcd mask suffice.
Total = Limit // 3
Top = (Limit // 2) isqrt
for M in 2 to Top
  Hi = (Limit // (2 * M) - M) min (M - 1)
  if Hi at least 1
    Ns = 1 to Hi array
    Co = Ns gcd M equal 1
    R = Ns filter (Co and ((M - Ns) mod 2 equal 1))
    Total += (Limit // (2 * M * (M + R))) sum
    E = Ns filter (Co and ((M - Ns) mod 3 not equal 0))
    Total += (Limit // ((2 * M + E) * (M + E))) sum
    Total += (Limit // (3 * M * (M + E))) sum
    Total += (Limit // ((2 * M + E) * (M + 2 * E))) sum
  end
end
Answer = Total
Answer print
